@name Explainer 2: best-form N-BK7 singlet 50mm f/4
# Explainer #2: the singlet of #1 bent to its best form for spherical
# aberration at f/4 (convex towards the object). Also shown stopped down to
# f/16 (#3).
# Role: bending spreads the work over both surfaces; spherical aberration drops.
# Design: both curvatures vary at fixed thickness and EFL 50 mm, minimising
# the 546 nm RMS spot on axis (object at 2.5 m).
# Rows match 01-singlet and 02b-flat-front.
